#N canvas 20 20 2520 1100 12;
#X text 20 20 alert-buffer-probe -- ANSWERED \, and kept as the re-check. A patch CAN draw into the ALERT buffer (screen 4) \, gFlip it \, and switch to it and back with setscreen. All of it works. g_oled still draws everything to screen 3 anyway -- see ref/module/display.md for why writable is not the same as safe., f 90;
#X text 20 110 Load it as a third patch after mother.pd and main.pd. It leaves the running patch alone: g_oled keeps drawing to screen 3 throughout \, and this only changes which buffer is SHOWN., f 90;
#X obj 20 210 loadbang;
#X obj 20 260 del 4000;
#X obj 20 300 t b b b;
#X msg 1400 350 drawing into buffer 4 then switching to it;
#X obj 1400 390 print PROBE;
#X msg 620 440 sendtyped /oled/gClear ii 4 1  \, sendtyped /oled/gBox iiiiii 4 0 0 127 63 1  \, sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiis 4 8 16 16 1 BUFFER-4  \, sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiis 4 8 44 8 1 buffer-4-works  \, sendtyped /oled/gFlip i 4  \, sendtyped /oled/setscreen i 4;
#X obj 620 490 s oscOut;
#X obj 20 580 del 6000;
#X obj 20 620 t b b;
#X msg 1400 670 switching back to screen 3 -- the meters should return;
#X obj 1400 710 print PROBE;
#X msg 620 760 sendtyped /oled/setscreen i 3;
#X obj 620 800 s oscOut;
#X text 20 870 WHAT IT SHOWED. BUFFER-4 appeared for six seconds and the live meters came back after it \, so writing \, flipping and switching an off-screen buffer all work. The alert layer did NOT move there. There was nothing to optimise -- g_oled rebuilds screen 3 from state ten times a second \, so nothing underneath needs preserving -- and switching is edge-triggered where every layer is state-driven \, so one lost setscreen strands the display on a device with no console. A dropped frame today self-corrects in 100 ms., f 90;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 2 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 4 1 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 4 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 10 1 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X connect 10 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
